# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# THIS IS THE PRIVATE REPO'S .gitignore. DO NOT COPY IT TO THE PUBLIC REPO.
#
# The public copy has an extra PUBLIC-REPO-ONLY block at the end that hides
# docs/unreleased/ and 19 internal design documents - 53 files in all. This
# file does NOT have it, so copying this repo wholesale into the public one
# replaces that block and publishes every one of them, permanently.
#
# To publish, build the tree with the script instead of by hand:
#     python tools/prepare-public.py <output-dir> --compare <public-checkout>
# It copies only what belongs in public, writes the correct .gitignore, and
# refuses to hand the tree over if anything held back slipped in.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# Build output and caches
.gradle/
build/
run/
out/
bin/

# IDE. bin/ above is the VS Code Java extension's output directory; these
# are the rest of what that extension and Eclipse drop into a project.
# NOTE gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar is deliberately NOT ignored: it
# is a tracked part of the wrapper and a clone cannot build without it.
.idea/
.vscode/
.project
.classpath
.settings/
.factorypath
*.iml

# JVM crash and profiling artifacts. This project runs real Minecraft
# clients constantly, and a crashed JVM writes these next to the working
# directory. A heap dump is hundreds of megabytes, so accidentally
# committing one is not a small mistake.
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log
.attach_pid*
*.hprof
*.log

# Machine-local configuration. Anything whose value is a path on one
# person's disk belongs here rather than in build.gradle: shipping such a
# path is exactly what stopped a clean clone from building before 1.0.0.
local.properties

# Operating system clutter
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Local tooling
__pycache__/
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# Staged release artifacts. Built from tags; never source of truth.
release/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# PUBLIC REPO ONLY. This block does not exist in the private repo, and it
# is the reason this .gitignore must not be overwritten by a straight copy
# of the private one. Over there these docs are tracked on purpose; here
# they must not be.
#
# Two reasons. Several carry a name the clean-room rule keeps out of
# anything public (NVIDIUM-ARCHITECTURE.md alone has 60 mentions), and the
# far-field files are designs for an unreleased 1.7 feature.
#
# The far-field CODE is still published, and has to be: it is compiled
# into the shipped jar, so it is part of the corresponding source whether
# or not a player can reach the feature. Only the design notes are held
# back.
#
# Ignore everything under docs/, then name the exceptions, so a new
# internal doc is private by default instead of public by accident.
docs/*
!docs/MODRINTH.md
!docs/PERFORMANCE.md
!docs/TECHNICAL.md
!docs/fps-chart.png
!docs/fps-chart-rd64.png
!docs/releases/
!docs/tools/
